    <help><![CDATA[
**What it does**

Runs a protein language model (ESM-2, ProtBERT, or ProtT5 -- auto-detected) in one of three modes: extract embeddings, train a classifier/regressor on embeddings, or LoRA/AdaLoRA fine-tune the encoder.

**Model source**

Select a model your Galaxy administrator has installed, or upload your own model archive (``.tgz``/``.tar`` of a Hugging Face model folder with safetensors weights).

**Train/test input (predict and fine-tune modes)**

Both modes take pre-split, tab-separated, 2-column tabular datasets (``sequence``, ``label``) -- a header row is expected but its column names are not checked. There is no internal train/test/validation splitting; use the ``sklearn_train_test_split`` tool beforehand if you need to split a single dataset.

**Per-residue (H5) output**

One dataset per sequence, keyed by a sanitised version of its FASTA id; the original id is kept as the dataset's ``original_id`` attribute::

    import h5py
    with h5py.File("output_embeddings.h5") as f:
        for key in f:
            residue_embeddings = f[key][:]
            original_id = f[key].attrs["original_id"]

**GPU**

Used automatically when available, otherwise runs on CPU.
